Title: "Special Operators"
Id: "e383d897-c838-49e6-bda0-87a290967d8f"

Text: "Special operators are not limited to single characters such as `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `=`, or `^`.

Any sequence of the operator characters `-~!#%^&*\+=|<>/` may be used as an operator. An operator run may also carry trailing prime marks and a `_`-prefixed subscript, so operators can be primed and indexed.

```mlg-fragment
*
**
+_-*
^^
*_1
*_free
*'
*''
*'_a
<=_max
```

A stropped symbolic name wraps an operator in backticks — `` `*` `` is the operator `*` referred to by name, and renders as `*` without the backticks.

A capability may also declare a **bracketed placeholder operator** `x_ [*] y_`, where `[*]` names a symbol drawn from the definition's inputs or `Defines:` target rather than a fixed character.

The directed forms `:*`, `*:`, and `:*:` apply to these operators as well."
Id: "07de0340-f3e8-4391-aa1b-4ed46cc466c2"
